        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0562" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">780.5/6–2354: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 217<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Pakistan</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d217-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-28T17:03:00-04:00">June 28, 1954—5:03
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1138. Re Embtel 1065.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d217-f2"/> You may inform Prime Minister we appreciate fact US
                    consulted prior Pakistan reply British suggestion regarding resumption general
                    UK-Pak conversations re Middle East defense. While US would not wish interpose
                    objection resumption talks initiated with Mirza we would strongly hope Pakistan authorities would treat as
                    tentative any views exchanged or interim conclusions reached. We would also
                    appreciate being informed nature of talks and views exchanged. We consider
                    period time will be required following arrival MAAG before careful analysis numerous problems directly or
                    indirectly affecting military posture Pakistan and Pakistan’s contribution to
                    Middle East defense can be completed.</p>
                <p>FYI only. We recognize from US point view further
                    evolution our own thinking regarding Middle East defense required. We are keenly
                    aware necessity early US–UK exchange views regarding Middle East defense but
                    inasmuch as we cannot predict exactly when such conversations will have been
                    completed and when we will be prepared enter detailed substantive discussions
                    this subject with Pakistanis we consider it unwise actively discourage
                    inclination Pakistan authorities accept present UK proposal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d217-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d217-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Anschuetz and cleared by BNA, SOA, and OFMA and
                        JCS of Defense. Repeated to London.</p>
            </note>
